// REJECTS: Field 'url' is required
//
// ModelConnectionParserGrammar has ONE definition rule shared by all three model
// connections: `(modelConnectionClass | connectionUrl | modelChainMappings)*`. Every field
// is optional and every field is legal in every one of them, as far as the grammar goes.
//
// What each connection actually requires is decided in the walker, per type: Json and Xml
// require class AND url, ModelChain requires mappings. So a generated parser accepts a
// JsonModelConnection with no url, an XmlModelConnection with `mappings:`, and a
// ModelChainConnection with a `class:` -- three different wrong models from one permissive
// rule. (The last two are accepted by legend-engine too; see the harness notes.)
###Connection
JsonModelConnection fixture::neg::NoUrl
{
   class: fixture::neg::Person;
}
